+## Git and path profile
+
+- On the planning APFS host, Apple Git 2.54.0 (Apple Git-157) accepted `--no-replace-objects --no-lazy-fetch --no-optional-locks`. PATH Git 2.42.1 refused `--no-lazy-fetch`. The fixed diff flag probe succeeded on both. Qualify the actual Git executable and version again at pickup with optional locks and replacements disabled. Use explicit offline object access or prove the repository is neither promisor nor partial before any object reads. Treat unsupported capability or ambiguous config/object storage as uncertainty.
+- Local repo config currently sets `core.precomposeUnicode=true`. The plan disables that setting in the raw-byte profile and checks actual directory-entry spelling on qualified APFS with a decomposed UTF-8 fixture. Record effective config, Git version and filesystem with the test. A name that cannot be safely represented yields uncertainty, and hosted raw non-UTF-8 fixtures exercise Git names without relying on the filesystem.
+- Reconfirm system/global config isolation, no optional index write, fixed diff/no driver profile, raw path handling, repository-only ignore sources, and no hidden fetch in the test fixtures. Keep local checkout identities and raw contents private.
